---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-border px-5 pb-24 pt-36 sm:pt-44">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
        <div class="text-small mb-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-brand/25 bg-brand/10 px-3 py-1 text-brand-strong">
          <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand"></span>
          Built for real Supabase workflows
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-display mx-auto max-w-4xl text-balance">
          Keep schema, seed data, and migrations in sync.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-body mx-auto mt-7 max-w-2xl text-balance text-muted-foreground">
          Supabee turns linked database dumps into reviewable files and replays migrations around your seed data in the right order.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/docs/getting-started/" class="text-label inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-foreground px-5 text-background shadow-lg transition hover:-translate-y-0.5">Get started</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/kaihochak/supabee" class="text-label inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-border bg-card px-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-brand/50">View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <div class="mx-auto mt-10 flex max-w-xl items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card/90 p-2 pl-5 text-left shadow-lg backdrop-blur">
          <span class="select-none font-mono text-brand">$</span>
          <code class="text-code-ui min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap font-mono">npm install -g supabee</code>
          <button data-copy="npm install -g supabee" class="text-small shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-5 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
        <div class="mb-12 max-w-2xl">
          <p class="text-overline mb-3 uppercase text-brand-strong">One focused workflow</p>
          <h2 class="text-title">From linked project to reproducible local state.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7">
            <span class="text-code-ui mb-8 flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-brand/12 font-mono text-brand-strong">01</span>
            <h3 class="text-heading">Sync</h3>
            <p class="text-body mt-2 text-muted-foreground">Dump schema or data from your linked Supabase project, then split, reconstruct, and validate it.</p>
            <code class="text-code-ui mt-6 block font-mono text-brand-strong">supabee sync schema</code>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7">
            <span class="text-code-ui mb-8 flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-brand/12 font-mono text-brand-strong">02</span>
            <h3 class="text-heading">Review</h3>
            <p class="text-body mt-2 text-muted-foreground">Keep generated SQL organized by schema category or table so changes stay readable in Git.</p>
            <code class="text-code-ui mt-6 block font-mono text-brand-strong">supabee migration audit</code>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7">
            <span class="text-code-ui mb-8 flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-brand/12 font-mono text-brand-strong">03</span>
            <h3 class="text-heading">Replay safely</h3>
            <p class="text-body mt-2 text-muted-foreground">Reset or start Supabase while deferring post-seed migrations and applying them afterward.</p>
            <code class="text-code-ui mt-6 block font-mono text-brand-strong">supabee db reset</code>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-border bg-muted/55 px-5 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[.85fr_1.15fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="text-overline mb-3 uppercase text-brand-strong">Predictable by design</p>
          <h2 class="text-title">The commands you need, without hiding the SQL.</h2>
          <p class="text-body mt-5 max-w-xl text-muted-foreground">Supabee orchestrates the official Supabase CLI and forwards commands it does not own. Your migrations and seed files remain ordinary SQL.</p>
          <a href="/docs/" class="text-label mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-brand-strong">Explore the documentation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-border bg-code text-code-foreground shadow-2xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-white/10 px-5 py-3">
            <span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-danger"></span><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-warning"></span><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-success"></span>
            <span class="text-code-ui ml-2 font-mono text-code-foreground/45">supabee</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="text-code-ui overflow-x-auto p-6 font-mono text-code-foreground/80"><code><span class="text-brand">$</span> supabee sync data
<span class="text-code-foreground/40">→</span> Checking linked migration alignment
<span class="text-code-foreground/40">→</span> Dumping data from linked project
<span class="text-code-foreground/40">→</span> Splitting data into per-table seed files
<span class="text-code-foreground/40">→</span> Reconstructing and validating output
<span class="text-success">✓</span> Data sync complete</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer class="text-small px-5 py-10 text-muted-foreground">
    <p class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">jacobchak © {new Date().getFullYear()}. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
